    description: "After PR 5 (WI-hamuk), Java scopes are labelled by:\n- method or constructor name plus hashed signature;\n- field or variable declarator name;\n- `new <Type>` for anonymous classes;\n- enum constant name.\n\nStill tied, split only by occurrence order:\n1. Two anonymous classes of one type that bind no name in one scope (`submit(new Runnable(){...})` twice). These are the 3 tie groups left in jedis.\n2. Same-named local classes in two blocks of one method.\n3. Anonymous classes in a `static {}` block and an instance `{}` block.\n\nAlso: Kotlin `object :` expressions share the anonymous-class defect (two `val`s of one type, two locals). Kotlin uses its own scope function; see WI-finam for the Kotlin locals sibling.\n\nRepros: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/hamuk/RESULTS.md and fixtures there."  # 02a7
